          "title": "You'll want to know: مول",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مول — mawwala — \"to fund\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مولت الدولة المشروع. mawwalat ad-dawla al-mashrūʿ. The state funded the project."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يمول, yumawwil."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun تمويل, tamwīl, funding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مول (mawwala) is built on the native Arabic root m-w-l, \"wealth, property\" (Lane). It is Form II of the root of māl, money: to provide with money, to fund."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
